==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Cooldown Equality}}

==Battleground==
*10 [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns.
*2 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 100~103.33 seconds<sup>3,000f~3,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Fallen Bear]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage has Teacher Bear variants that easily push, and Nyandam variants that can nuke your units if you were to push too far. Due to the severe lack of peons, a [[Battle Items|Rich Cat]] is recommended.

[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] excel like most of the stages here, although tankers are required to not let them get immediately killed.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: At level 32, Can Can Cat survives a Teacher Bear hit, and survives one at level 39 on 2♛. With Extra Money and Move Speed Up, Can Can Cat can secure at least one hit on Teacher Bear, greatly weakening it and potentially giving a huge income boost. Can also land some free hits on the Nyandams if given the chance.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Can be used similarly to Can Can Cat, as they can land free hits on Teacher Bear and the Nyandam variants. However, it cannot survive a Teacher Bear hit, so be sure to time it well.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: As mentioned previously, both units excel here, being easily stackable due to their greatly decreased cooldowns while allowing you to gain ground. Make sure to protect them well however, as they will easily die to any attack here.
*[[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]]: Can brush off hits from the Ursamajors and Galatic Overseer Nyandam, but can't do much otherwise.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]: The most accessible unit that can break Fallen Bear's shield. Be sure to not let it push too far, as it will easily die to any attack. This is mostly remedied by its decreased cooldown.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: If your units were to get nuked, Stone Cat can easily allow you to regain ground, keeping the enemies in place for a short amount of time that might be able to save your run.



